.TH SDL_StepBackUTF8 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_StepBackUTF8 \- Decode a UTF-8 string in reverse, one Unicode codepoint at a time.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "Uint32 SDL_StepBackUTF8(const char *start, const char **pstr);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This will go to the start of the previous Unicode codepoint in the string, move
.BR *pstr
to that location and return that codepoint\[char46]
.PP
If
.BR *pstr
is already at the start of the string), it will not advance
.BR *pstr
at all\[char46]
.PP
Generally this function is called in a loop until it returns zero, adjusting its parameter each iteration\[char46]
.PP
If an invalid UTF-8 sequence is encountered, this function returns
.BR SDL_INVALID_UNICODE_CODEPOINT \[char46]
.PP
Several things can generate invalid UTF-8 sequences, including overlong encodings, the use of UTF-16 surrogate values, and truncated data\[char46] Please refer to
.URL https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3629.txt RFC3629
for details\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I start
a pointer to the beginning of the UTF-8 string\[char46]
.TP
.I pstr
a pointer to a UTF-8 string pointer to be read and adjusted\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the previous Unicode codepoint in the string\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

